hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1054","Yahya bin Habib Al-Harithi told us, on the authority of Hammad, meaning Ibn Zaid, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub, on the authority of Ismail, who is the son of Abraham, Khalid told us, and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, Ibn Ulayya, told us, Khaled told us Al-Hadha’, H. Al-Sana’ani and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, H., narrated to us Bundar, Abd al-Wahhab told us, meaning al-Thaqafi, Khalid al-Hadha’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him in three rak’ahs of the afternoon prayer, then he got up and entered the room, and Al-Kharbaq, a man with simple hands, stood up. Then he called him: O Messenger of God, has the prayer been shortened? So he came out angry, dragging his garment. He asked and was told. He prayed that prayer which he had neglected, then he prostrated. He prostrated two times, then he saluted.” This is the wording of the hadith of Bundar. Others said: Then he said the salutation, then he prostrated two prostrations, then he said the salutation."
